  "worked_solution": "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-9,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =(-9){(x-3)}^{2} \\\\  & =-9(x-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(x-3)^{2} & =-9({x}^{2}-6x+9) \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}+54x-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-9{x}^{2}+54x-81.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
